8. 🔐 Security / Anti-Spam
  Watch designated "OH GOD THE SPAM BOT IS HERE" channel
  Automatically ban users who post there
  Audit everything Ratburn does


Handling Punishment
  Punishment
    ├── ID
    ├── User
    ├── Type
    ├── Reason
    ├── Demerits awarded
    ├── Date issued
    ├── Issued by
    ├── Status
    ├── Start time
    ├── End time
    ├── Related detention visit
    ├── Override reason
    └── Override timestamp
  
  Detention Visit
    ├── ID
    ├── User
    ├── Triggering punishment
    ├── Start
    ├── End
    ├── Reason
    ├── Status
    └── Notes
  
  /discipline override <punishment> <reason>: Mod+ command that overrides user's punishment (forgive).
  /discipline pardon: Admin command that reverts punishment when unfairly punished (forget).
  /discipline active: Mod+ command showing currently active punishments.

Birthdays
    user_id
    month
    day
    birth_year (nullable)
    So:
    No year
    🎂 Happy Birthday, @User!
    Year provided
    Ratburn calculates their age on that birthday, rather than storing a static age.
    Which means the database never needs updating.
    And the calendar command could produce:
    🎂 October Birthdays
    October 3 — @User1
    October 14 — @User2
    October 14 — @User3
    October 29 — @User4
    Make the year never appear in the public calendar.

Audit
  Everything significant should be logged.
  Not necessarily every normal bot message, but administrative state changes.
  Something like:
    Action	Example
    ROLE_ADD	Ratburn assigned Detention
    ROLE_REMOVE	Detention expired
    DEMERIT_ADD	+2 demerits
    PUNISHMENT_CREATE	New punishment
    PUNISHMENT_OVERRIDE	Mod overturned punishment
    BAN	User banned
    UNBAN	User unbanned
    FILTER_ADD	5 words added
    FILTER_REMOVE	Word removed
    EVENT_CREATE	Event scheduled
    EVENT_EDIT	Event modified
    EVENT_CANCEL	Event cancelled
    BIRTHDAY_UPDATE	User changed birthday
    CONFIG_CHANGE	Ratburn settings changed
  
  And every audit record should have:
    timestamp
    actor
    action
    target
    details

Setup
  Proper setup system.
  Instead of making the admin manually configure 900 things in a database, eventually:
    /ratburn setup
  and Ratburn walks them through it.
  
  Something like:
    Mr. Ratburn's Setup Assistant  
    Let's get this classroom in order.
    1/8 — Moderation
      Please select the role used for moderators.
      Then:
        2/8 — Detention
        Select the Detention role.
      Then:
        3/8 — Detention Channel
        Select the channel.
      etc.

**Every** table gets a guild_id.

CONTENT v CONFIG
  Configuration
    Things like:
      Detention role
      Detention channel
      Moderator role
      Admin role
      Protected channel
      Server timezone
      Demerit thresholds
      Punishment durations
      AFK timeout
  
  Content
    Things like:
      Filter words
      Quiz questions
      Ratburn responses
      Magic trick GIFs
      Birthday messages
      Bot explanations
  That way /ratburn config and /ratburn content can be cleanly distinct.
